# Parallax high-value 4-layer VM rules (APK-only v2)
#
# Pass this file with:
#   java -jar parallax.jar -f app.apk --high-value-methods parallax-high-value-methods.rules
#
# Canonical signature syntax:
#   Lpackage/name/Class;->method(ARGS)RETURN
#
# Four virtualization stages are applied to every successfully selected method:
#   L1: Dalvik -> semantic VM IR
#   L2: register permutation + randomized decoy micro-ops
#   L3: shuffled state-machine cells with random state IDs
#   L4: encoded opcode/register/word cells interpreted natively with per-cell guards
#
# v2 intentionally supports only:
#   - static methods
#   - 0..4 int (I) parameters
#   - int (I) or void (V) return
#   - deterministic integer arithmetic / bitwise / branch bytecode
#   - no objects, arrays, field access, invokes, monitor, switch payloads, or try/catch
#
# A selected method that is unsupported, or a rule that matches nothing, FAILS the pack.
# There is no silent fallback to the normal DEX method vault.
#
# Examples (replace with real methods from your own APK):
# Lcom/example/security/LicenseMath;->mix(III)I
# Lcom/example/security/TokenMath;->scramble(IIII)I
# Lcom/example/security/StateMath;->advance(II)V
#
# '*' and '?' wildcards are supported, but exact signatures are recommended for high-value code.
